id: SECRETS-055
title: Firebase Cloud Messaging Server Key
category: secrets
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .tsx .js .jsx .py .java .go .rb .rs .cpp .h .cs .php .env .yml .yaml .json .toml .xml .properties .cfg .ini .conf .sh .tf .hcl
  exclude_paths: test/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/ __pycache__/ .venv/ target/
patterns:
  - regex: AAAA[A-Za-z0-9_-]{7}:[A-Za-z0-9_-]{140}
    message: Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM) server key detected. This allows sending push notifications to any device registered with your app.
fix: Migrate to FCM v1 API which uses service account credentials. Delete the legacy server key in Firebase Console > Project Settings > Cloud Messaging.
